# Plugin / Extension System Skeleton (Permanent)

## Law

**Core block registry stays authoritative.** Plugins only **extend** it via compiled first-party manifests — never by evaluating tenant-uploaded code.

| Concern | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| Manifest | `id`, `version`, `blocks[]`, optional `moduleCode` (plugin-level gate) |
| Block types | Must match `plugin.[a-z][a-z0-9_]*` — never collide with core/module types |
| Load path | `packages/plugins` (`@vdb/plugins`) — allowlisted first-party only |
| Trust | `trust: first-party` only in MVP |
| Unknown blocks | Renderer **fail-safe** (skip / placeholder) — never crash PDF/preview workers |

## Security (locked)

- **No** `eval` / `Function` / dynamic `import()` of user- or Business-supplied JS.
- **No** remote plugin marketplace download / unsigned packages in this skeleton.
- Third-party / signed plugins require a **new ADR** reversing this non-goal.

## Runtime

1. Boot loads `loadFirstPartyPlugins()` → `registerPluginBlocks` in `@vdb/document-schema`.
2. `getBlockRegistry()` = built-in `BLOCK_REGISTRY` + registered plugin entries.
3. Validate / collect module codes against `getBlockRegistry()`.
4. API: `GET /api/plugins` lists manifests (JWT). Editor palette uses effective registry.

## Editions

Available on **both** `SAAS` and `SELF_HOSTED` (first-party extensions ship in the artifact).

## Non-goals (skeleton)

- Seller-published plugins, WASM sandboxes, per-Business custom script upload.
- Per-plugin billing SKUs beyond existing `module.*` / entitlement on declared `moduleCode`.
